Package: command
Type: Package
Title: Process Command Line Arguments
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "John",
           family = "Bryant",
	   email = "john@bayesiandemography.com",
	   role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Bayesian Demography Limited",
            role = "cph"))
Description: Process command line arguments. Processing includes
    checking arguments, matching arguments to names,
    and converting strings to numbers, booleans, or dates.
    The main function, cmd_assign(), allows the inputs and outputs
    of a file to be clearly defined, leading to
    safer, more modular data analysis pipelines.
